DESIGN AUTHORITY: The user's requirements determine the programme, site, style and scale. Choose from the brief, not a preset menu. Independently choose composition, footprint, levels, roof forms, facade organization, materials and outdoor relationships. Neither assemblies, stored recipes nor previous projects prescribe these choices. Simple or complex architecture is valid when justified by the brief. Record the selected design and its constructed relationships; no preset concepts or alternative-count requirement applies. Preserve required accommodation capacity and requested features; disclose unbuilt portions instead of shrinking the brief. Exterior scope defers interior fit-out.

